  <!-- RH56E2 hands. Hand-written, unlike the block above, and the one part of this file
       that is a guess: the pairs below were not read from move_group's contacts, because the
       hand meshes were not available. Two categories.

       Every pair of links inside one hand (reason User). The vendor's finger meshes overlap
       at the joints and the mechanism cannot drive them into each other, so a self-collision
       check inside the hand can only report noise. This includes finger against finger, which
       is what stops a closed posture from being rejected for fingers touching the palm.

       The hand's base and palm against the wrist (reason User), the one hand-to-arm pair the
       old Dex3 block also carried. Others may be needed once the meshes are in: run
       /check_state_validity at the rest pose, as README.md describes, and add whatever it
       reports. Cross-hand and hand-to-body pairs are deliberately left checked. -->
